<div class="content-box centerer">
    <h2>
        What is UniConnect?
    </h2>
    <p>
        <%= @whatIs %>
    </p>
</div>
<div class="content-box centerer">
    <h2>
        How to use UniConnect
    </h2>
    <p>
        <%= @howTo %>
    </p>
</div>
<div class="content-box centerer">
    <h2>
        What is UniConnect's Purpose?
    </h2>
    <p>
        Through UniConnect we aim to provide an efficient and effective matching service between would-be mentors and mentees. This should allow students at the University of Sheffield an opportunity to gain more knowledge and/or help about studying or university life in general.
    </p>
</div>
<div class="content-box centerer">
    <h2>
        Who are we?
    </h2>
    <p>
        We are Team 17, a group of students at the University of Sheffield, who are developing this web app to pass a module. We think this website is a very good idea and we will try to make it work well. If you need help, support or further information, please contact us or read through the relevant pages via the dropdown menu at the top right corner of this (and all other) page(s).
    </p>
</div>

<% if @accountType == "admin" %>
    <div class="content-box centerer">
        <h2>
            How to use UniConnect's admin portal?
        </h2>
        <h3>
            Access each administrative tool via the left menu:
        </h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                New Users approval - All new accounts must be approved by administrators before they can join the mentoring scheme. This tool allows you to 
                filter users by admins, mentors, or mentees and accept or reject their applications. Admins require additional attention, including setting a 
                password, which you must then inform the user about in person.
                </li>
            <li>
                Manage accounts - You can filter users by email, name, or ID. Clicking on a user will display their profile details, where you can 
                toggle the mentor badge and adjust the global maximum mentees for mentors, and view the current password of the user in case they have forgotten it.
            </li>
            <li>
                Flagging & deletion - If an account has violated the terms & conditions, you can flag an account here (you must provide a reason). In extenuating 
                circumstances, accounts can also be deleted.
            </li>
            <li>
                Matches - If a matched user encounters issues and their mentorship needs to be terminated, you can manually unmatch and match mentors and mentees.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Don’t forget to check your emails for any support tickets from users!</h3>
    <% end %>
</div>